                <pb facs="0895" n="800" sameAs="frus:frus1936v04/pg800"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">894.6363/296: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-12-17T11:00:00+09:00">December 17, 1936—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 17—2:40 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>261. Embassy’s 259, December 14, 1 p.m.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>The <hi rendition="#italic">Asahi</hi> this morning reports that the
                        Japanese oil companies are agitating against the granting of any increases
                        in the gasoline sales quotas by the Ministry of Commerce and Industry to the
                        foreign oil companies because (<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>) the purpose
                        of the petroleum industry law is to protect the Japanese oil industry and
                        therefore the quotas of foreign companies should not be increased and (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">b</hi>) the foreign oil companies have as yet failed
                        to fulfill the oil storage obligation. The newspaper adds that the question
                        is expected to become an issue in the coming session of the Diet.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>The above is transmitted as a further indication of the situation with
                        which the foreign oil interests are faced in Japan.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
